# Foundation — no hardcoded layout (law)

When sizing, spacing, radius, type scale, or density for **foundation paint** (catalog cards, event cards, chrome, shell density):

| Do | Don’t |
|----|--------|
| Put reused numbers in `packages/forja_foundation/lib/tokens/*` | Magic `0.85`, `130.0`, `220.0` in widgets / host paint |
| Read `ShellTokens` / `DetailsTokens` / `EventCardTokens` / sibling `*Tokens` | Copy a literal that already exists on a token |
| Add a named token when introducing a new density or clamp | Inline scale/clamp next to `cardWidth` / `cardHeight` |

```dart
// ❌
return (base * 0.85).clamp(130.0, 165.0);

// ✅ — EventCardTokens (or the matching *Tokens file)
return (base * EventCardTokens.desktopWidthScale).clamp(
  EventCardTokens.desktopHeightMin,
  EventCardTokens.desktopHeightMax,
);
```

**Where tokens live**

| Surface | Token file |
|---------|------------|
| Shell / catalog density | `forja_shell_tokens.dart` |
| Media details | `forja_details_tokens.dart` |
| Live event / match cards | `event_card_tokens.dart` |
| Other reusable chrome | sibling `*_tokens.dart` in `tokens/` |

One-off padding inside a single private widget is fine. **Grid min size, aspect clamps, play overlay diameter, paint fallbacks** are not one-offs — token them.

Host kit paint (`paint_artifact`, catalog grids) must import foundation tokens — never re-hardcode the same numbers in `apps/forja`.

See also: [forja-design-system.mdc](./forja-design-system.mdc).
